{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773343309,"nonce":"XavGqnnR7r/hoza7BQUCitcfRz0=","title":"mandible: unified chat history search CLI across Claude/Gemini/Codex","message":"Add `mandible search` (or `mandible chat search`) CLI subcommand providing unified, filterable search across all agent chat logs.\n\n## Motivation\nCurrently searching chat logs requires manual grepping of provider-specific files (Claude JSONL, Gemini JSON, Codex sessions). Each has a different format. A unified CLI would:\n- Abstract over provider formats\n- Allow cross-model searches in one command\n- Enable efficient agent use (fewer tool calls vs iterative grep)\n\n## Design questions to resolve\n\n**Storage layer:**\nOption A: Search provider files directly with a per-provider parser (lazy, no extra storage)\nOption B: Normalize and cache to SQLite/own format on ingest (enables fast indexed search, but requires ongoing sync)\nOption C: Normalize to flat JSON files per conversation (easily greppable, no DB needed)\n\nThe Mandible conversations scanner may already do some normalization — check `src/routes/conversations.ts` and related.\n\n**Normalized block types (for filter flags):**\n- `--user` / `--assistant` — filter by role\n- `--thinking` — include/exclude thinking blocks\n- `--tool-use` / `--tool-result` — include/exclude tool calls\n- `--provider claude|gemini|codex|all` — filter by source\n\n**CLI sketch:**\n```\nmandible search \"query\" [--provider claude|gemini|codex|all] [--role user|assistant] [--thinking] [--since 7d] [--limit 20]\n```\n\n**Feasibility check needed:**\n- Does Mandible already normalize conversation blocks across providers?\n- Are Gemini/Codex conversation files accessible and parseable?\n- Is grep-on-files fast enough, or does indexed search matter at typical corpus sizes?","files":null}]}